# ============================================================================
# Authentication Configuration
# ============================================================================

# The server automatically detects the authentication method:
# - If FABRIC_CLIENT_SECRET is set: Uses Service Principal authentication
# - If FABRIC_CLIENT_SECRET is not set: Uses Interactive authentication (device code flow)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 1: Interactive Authentication (Recommended for Individual Users)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave all values below commented out or unset. The server will use:
# - Default Power BI client ID
# - 'common' tenant (works with any Microsoft account)
# - Device code flow for authentication

# Optional: Uncomment to use a custom Azure AD app for interactive auth
# FABRIC_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
# FABRIC_TENANT_ID=your_tenant_id_here

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 2: Service Principal Authentication (For Automation/CI-CD)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment all three values below to use service principal authentication:
# FABRIC_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
# FABRIC_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here
# FABRIC_TENANT_ID=your_tenant_id_here
